    <string name="workshop_prueba_descripcion_tps_barrido">With the engine off and the ignition on, move the throttle through five positions while the app reads the TPS at the maximum rate. Each position is compared with its reference range, and the slow sweep looks for dropouts, spikes and dead spots.</string>
    <string name="workshop_prueba_descripcion_minimo_retorno">With the engine running in neutral, record 45 s of idle without touching the throttle, then rev to about 3,000 rpm three times and release sharply: it measures whether the idle holds, how far it drops on release and whether the engine stalls.</string>
    <string name="workshop_prueba_descripcion_arranque_frio">After sitting overnight: compares the engine temperature with the air temperature with the ignition on, counts the starting attempts and follows the warm-up to 60 °C or until you tap Finish.</string>
    <string name="workshop_prueba_descripcion_bateria_carga">Reads the adapter voltage (AT RV) as fast as it responds: the battery at rest with the ignition on, the drop while cranking, and charging at idle and at higher revs. If the adapter resets while cranking, it is recorded as a finding.</string>
    <string name="workshop_prueba_descripcion_map_baro">With the engine off there is no vacuum, so the MAP should read barometric pressure. It is compared with the ECU reading (PID 33), the phone barometer or an estimate from GPS altitude, each with its own margin.</string>
